.Dd 2026-11-07
.Dt LBTS 1
.\" Manual page created by:
.\" Guus Sliepen <guus@lightbts.info>
.Sh NAME
.Nm lbts
.Nd the command line interface for LightBTS
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl dhv
.Op Fl -batch
.Op Fl -data-dir Ar path
.Op Fl -help
.Op Fl -json
.Op Fl -link Ar type Ns Op : Ns Ar id
.Op Fl -no-email
.Op Fl -sort Ar field
.Op Fl -no-hooks
.Op Fl -version
.Ar command ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This the command line interface for LightBTS, a light-weight issue tracking system.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl -batch
Force batch mode.
No interactive input will be used, and the output will not be piped through a pager.
Batch mode is enabled automatically if stdin or stdout is not an interactive terminal.
.It Fl d, -data-dir Ar path
Set the path to the LightBTS data.
This can also be controlled by setting the
.Ev LIGHTBTS_DIR
environment variable.
.It Fl h, -help
Print the synopsis and a list of the supported commands, then exit.
.It Fl -json
Write the output of
.Nm lbts list ,
.Nm lbts show
and
.Nm lbts fields
as JSON, see
.Sx JSON OUTPUT .
.It Fl v, -verbose
Show more details, for example the full text of all messages in
.Nm lbts show .
.It Fl m, -message Ar text
Use the given text as the message instead of invoking an editor or reading it from stdin.
.It Fl F, -field Ar field Ns = Ns Ar value
Set a field of a new ticket or reply.
This option can be specified multiple times.
.It Fl S, -severity Ar severity
Set the severity of a new ticket or reply.
.It Fl T, -tag Ar tag
Add a tag. This option can be specified multiple times.
.It Fl V Ar version
Record a version. This option can be specified multiple times.
.It Fl A, -attach Ar file
Attach a file to the message. This option can be specified multiple times.
.It Fl -link Ar type : Ns Ar id
Link a new ticket or reply to another ticket, for example
.Ql --link blocks:12 .
This option can be specified multiple times.
For
.Nm lbts tree ,
the type of links to follow.
.It Fl -sort Ar field
Sort the tickets of
.Nm lbts list
and
.Nm lbts tree
by a field,
.Ql title
or
.Ql number .
With a leading
.Ql - ,
sort in descending order.
The default is set by the
.Va cli.sort
configuration variable, and is the ticket number if that is not set.
.It Fl -depth Ar n
For
.Nm lbts tree ,
the number of levels to show.
.It Fl -markdown
For
.Nm lbts tree ,
write Markdown.
.It Fl -no-email
Disable sending any emails during the execution of the command.
.It Fl -no-hooks
Disable running any hooks during the execution of the command.
.It Fl -version
Print version information and exit.
.El
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It close Ar id
Close a ticket.
.It config Ar variable Op Ar value
Get or set a configuration option.
.It create Ar title
Create a new ticket.
.It deadline Ar id Ar deadline
Change the deadline of a ticket.
.It describe Ar id
Replace the description of a ticket.
.It fields
Show the definitions of the fields of tickets.
.It fixed Ar id Ar version
Record the version where a problem is fixed.
.It found Ar id Ar version
Record the version where a problem is found.
.It fsck
Check the messages and the index for problems.
.It get Ar id Ar field
Print the values of a field of a ticket, one per line.
.It help Op Ar command
If a
.Ar command
is specified, show the manual page for the given command.
Otherwise, print the synopsis and a list of the supported commands.
.It import Op Ar file ...
Import one or more messages into the database.
.It init Op Ar directory
Initialize a LightBTS instance.
.It link Ar id1 Ar type Ar id2
Add a link of the given type between two tickets.
.It list Oo Ar selector ... Oc Op Ar field
List tickets, or the values of a field that these tickets use, as in
.Ql lbts list open tags .
The selectors are described in
.Xr lbts-fields 5 .
The fields shown for each ticket are set by the
.Va cli.columns
configuration variable, and are status and severity by default.
.It milestone Ar id
Change the milestone of a ticket
.It noowner Ar id
Remove ownership of a ticket.
.It notfixed Ar id Ar version
Remove records of where a problem is fixed.
.It notfound Ar id Ar version
Remove records of where a problem is found.
.It owner Ar id Ar name
Change the ownership of a ticket.
.It progress Ar id Ar percentage
Change the progress of a ticket.
.It reopen Ar id
Reopen a ticket.
.It reindex
Rebuild the index from the stored messages.
.It reply Ar id
Reply to an existing ticket.
.It retitle Ar id Ar title
Change the title of a ticket.
.It set Ar id Ar field Ar value ...
Change a field of a ticket.
.It severity Ar id Ar severity
Change the severity of a ticket.
.It show Ar id
Show ticket or message details.
.It tags Ar id Oo +|- Oc Ar tag ...
Add tags to or remove tags from a ticket.
.It tree Oo Ar id Oc Op Ar selector ...
Show a ticket and the tickets it depends on, recursively.
.It unlink Ar id1 Ar type Ar id2
Remove a link of the given type between two tickets.
.It unset Ar id Ar field
Unset a field of a ticket.
.It version
Print version information.
.El
.Pp
The commands severity, tags, owner, noowner, milestone, deadline and progress
are shortcuts for set and unset, and only work if the corresponding field exists.
.Pp
Errors are reported on stderr, and result in exit code 1.
Problems with pseudo-headers, such as an invalid severity, are reported as warnings,
but the message is still recorded.
.Sh TICKETS
Each ticket has a number and an ID.
Numbers are assigned in the order tickets are created,
but only in the instance where they are created:
another copy of the same tickets, for example in another clone of a git repository,
can number them differently.
The ID is the same everywhere: it is the BLAKE2b hash of the Message-ID of the ticket's first message,
which is also the name of the file of that message.
It is shown as its shortest unique prefix, but at least 7 characters.
.Pp
Commands accept a ticket number, optionally preceded by
.Ql # ,
a prefix of at least 4 characters of an ID,
or the Message-ID of any message of the ticket.
Messages that
.Nm
writes refer to other tickets by their ID.
.Sh JSON OUTPUT
With
.Fl -json ,
.Nm lbts list
writes an array of tickets.
Each ticket is an object with the members
.Va id
(the full ID),
.Va short_id ,
.Va number ,
.Va title
and
.Va fields .
The fields are an object with the values of the fields that are set:
an array for set fields, an integer for number fields, and a string otherwise.
If
.Nm lbts list
lists the values of a field, it writes an array of these values instead.
.Pp
.Nm lbts show
writes a single ticket, with the additional members
.Va submitter ,
.Va date
(in ISO 8601 format, in UTC),
.Va versions
(with the arrays
.Va found
and
.Va fixed ) ,
.Va links
and
.Va linked_from
(arrays of objects with the link
.Va type
and the
.Va id ,
.Va short_id ,
.Va number
and
.Va title
of the other ticket),
and
.Va messages
(an array of objects with the members
.Va message_id ,
.Va from ,
.Va to ,
.Va subject
and
.Va date ,
and with
.Fl v
also
.Va text ) .
For a Message-ID, it writes that message, with its text, and the ticket it belongs to as
.Va ticket .
.Pp
.Nm lbts fields
writes an array of field definitions, with the same names as the variables in
.Xr lbts-fields 5 .
.Pp
Strings that are not valid UTF-8 have the invalid bytes replaced by U+FFFD.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Ev EDITOR
Use the given command for interactive editing of messages.
.It Ev EMAIL
If set,
.Nm
will use the given email address in the "From:" header of the messages it creates.
.It Ev FULLNAME
If set,
.Nm
will use the given name in the "From:" header of the messages it creates.
.It Ev LIGHTBTS_DIR
Set the path to the LightBTS data.
.It Ev LIGHTBTS_PAGER
This environment variable overrides
.Ev PAGER .
.It Ev PAGER
Use the given command to pipe output through when running interactively.
If both
.Ev PAGER
and
.Ev LIGHTBTS_PAGER
are not set, the default will be to use
.Xr less 1 .
If
.Ev PAGER
is set to an empty string, to "-" or to "cat",
.Nm
will not launch a pager.
.It Ev VISUAL
This environment variable overrides
.Ev EDITOR .
.It Ev XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
If set,
.Nm
will use the given directory for storing temporary files.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Nm
will store and retrieve files from a directory named
.Pa .lightbts ,
unless overridden by the environment variable
.Ev LIGHTBTS_DIR
or by the command line option
.Fl d
or
.Fl -data-dir .
If not overridden, it will first look for
.Pa .lightbts
in the current directory.
If it cannot find it there, it will try if that directory exists in the parent directory,
and so on until it reaches the root directory.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr lbts-fields 5 ,
.Xr lbts-hooks 5 ,
.Xr lightbts 7 .
